Apply the FP8 multi-query 3D path to the target's attention only, leaving the
draft on the unmodified path, behind its own opt-in.

The build produces target-only views; the original metadata and the KV writes
stay intact. Adaptive verification can rewrite individual GPU query boundaries
without changing their CPU mirrors, so those views are never sliced by CPU
offsets, and padding, malformed boundaries and non-contiguous phases are
rejected rather than reshaped.

This switch shapes the graph and is deliberately NOT excluded from
compile_factors.

